## Model orchestration

For substantial or risky multi-model work, use `$model-orchestration`. Its `model-routing.md` reference owns the current pool metadata, capability constraints, and adaptive routing policy.

- Select per call from every compatible, enabled non-Haiku model; no model owns a task role or provider sequence.
- Use the routing owner's evidence-based selection axes and bounded review policy. Ratings and bootstrap efforts are priors, not assignments.
- The current session owns scope, synthesis, validation, and acceptance. Workers and reviewers are leaves unless it explicitly authorizes fan-out.
- When running non-interactively through `codex exec` under another orchestrator, implement the assigned task directly and do not re-delegate; the parent owns planning and review.
